n despite it being the platform's  most requested feature social media  experts told me on twitter things are  slightly more complicated where people  follow politicians and thought leaders  every word and since tweets are public  by default posts on twitter can go viral  a lot more quickly than they might have  on other platforms lots of users see  twitter as a hub of political discourse  and for news and just like in the old  days once you put it out there you can't  go back and change what you said users  see that as a way of holding people and  institutions accountable for what they  post but the ability to edit tweets  would allow tweeters to dial back  language it also allows them to double  down on their message if it starts to go  viral and for a long time twitter did  not want to change just two years ago  twitter's ceo at the time jack dorsey  said that an edit button was unlikely in  twitter's future but it turns out  twitter has been working on an edit  button since last year though not  everyone is excited about the  possibility of an edit button people  against an edit button argue that it  could be used to make more substantial  changes a user could revise a tweet  after it's gone viral completely  altering its meaning and potentially  misleading other users for active users  the news of a potential edit button  could mean a few things visually it  might look something like this mock-up  twitter released  [Music]  also twitter says it's figuring out how  to add parameters so it might work  differently than how it does on facebook  and instagram one idea the company has  is to create time restraints so you  would only be able to edit a post within  a certain window of time twitter could  also add other signifiers showing that a  tweet was changed and it could restrict  the amount of characters you're allowed  to alter the company's head of consumer  product jay sullivan tweeted this  without things like time limits controls  and transparency about what has been  edited edit could be misused to alter  the record of the public conversation  but if you want the tool you'll have to  pay at least at first twitter is beta  testing it in the coming months for  people who sign up for twitter blue it's  a subscription service for 299 a month  that gives you more ways to manage your  twitter account and it'll also let you  customize the app twitter declined to  comment beyond its public tweets if  you're like me and barely tweet an edit  button might not mean so much you may  occasionally run into someone trying to  abuse the new feature by tweeting  something obnoxious to drive up their  engagement and then changing it to  something more mild i mean it is social  media after all but at least you'll be  able to keep misspelled words from  lingering around on your profile for all  of eternity  you
 

